    decision:
      "Unattended scheduled routine (\"continue toward a profitable and growing business, merge changes when done\"), picked up at origin/main tip 09f7ae4 (PR #641, buffer-entitlement-gate-docs-disclosure) on branch claude/upbeat-dijkstra-ijcc7s — the session's local clone started shallow with no merge-base against origin/main; ran `git fetch --unshallow` before trusting any divergence count, after which the branch matched origin/main's tip exactly. Confirmed baseline green: npm ci (409 packages, 0 vulnerabilities) + npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run (2650 passed, 198 files). mcp__github__list_pull_requests reconfirmed the sole open PR is still #202 (unrelated human draft). Fold-scanned remote branches after a full `git fetch origin '+refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*' --prune` (580 refs): diffed the newest 10 claude/* siblings against origin/main — every one is either a pure process-log-only diff or byte-identical to content already merged under a different SHA (PRs #634-#641, including the large upbeat-dijkstra-sm4qyg Buffer-scaffold orphan) — no live fold candidate.\n\nDispatched a foreground general-purpose research agent, briefed on AGENT_PROTOCOL + NEXT_STEPS + recent ITERATIONS, to hunt a fresh gap on the newest-shipped surface (the Buffer auto-posting scaffold, five straight iterations of spot-checks on its edges) and the Stripe Connect scaffold. It found a real, previously-unflagged bug: scheduleMarketingPackToBufferAction (src/app/dashboard/leads/actions.ts) selected a variant to post via `pack.variants.find((v) => v.contentType === contentType)` — `.find()` always returns the FIRST matching element. MONTHLY_MARKETING_PACK_TYPES (src/lib/marketing/monthly-pack.ts) generates 3 facebook_caption and 3 instagram_caption variants per lead per UTC month (the sold Growth/Complete deliverable, /docs/marketing-automation's own content-type-count table says 3), so every 'Send pack to Buffer' click — no matter how many times clicked — could only ever queue variant #1 of 3; the other two Facebook and two Instagram pieces generated and billed for that month were structurally unreachable through this feature (only visible via the manual per-variant Copy buttons in the same panel, which correctly iterate all variants). The UI's own copy ('Posts this month's facebook_caption / instagram_caption variants...') and the docs page both already described the intended behavior as plural/all-variants, confirming this was a bug in the implementation, not an intentional 'send one representative post' design. I independently verified by reading monthly-pack.ts's MONTHLY_MARKETING_PACK_TYPES array, the buggy `.find()` call site, bufferServiceContentType's facebook/instagram-only mapping, and both the dashboard panel copy and docs prose before fixing.",
    rationale:
      "This is precisely AGENT_PROTOCOL's tier-1 'sold-capability wiring gap' class: a computed, persisted, billed-for asset (2 of every 3 Facebook/Instagram variants generated each month) was reachable only through the manual Copy-button fallback, not through the auto-post feature whose entire stated purpose (per the marketing-content-scheduling NEXT_STEPS entry) is to replace operator copy-paste. Fixed by changing `.find()` to `.filter()` and looping over every matching variant per profile, queuing each with its own createBufferUpdate call (Buffer's classic API schedules into the profile's existing posting slots, never posts immediately, so multiple queued updates per profile is the correct behavior, not a burst-post risk). The scheduled/failed result arrays now label each entry `${profileId} (${index + 1}/${variants.length})` when a profile has more than one matching variant, so a partial-month queue (e.g. 2 of 3 succeeded, 1 failed) is visible in the operator-facing result rather than reading as a flat success/failure per profile. Deliberately NOT shipped this iteration: persistent per-variant duplicate-post prevention across repeated clicks (e.g. re-clicking 'Send pack to Buffer' a second time within the same month re-queues all 3 variants again, since nothing marks a specific variant as already-posted) — that requires a new persisted marker (contentType+index or a content hash, per lead+profile+month) and is a distinct, larger follow-up left for a future iteration rather than folded into this fix, matching this log's established scoping discipline (one focused iteration per run). Updated both docs surfaces that described the old (buggy) singular behavior: /docs/marketing-automation's Buffer paragraph now says 'queues every matching variant... all 3 of each, matching MONTHLY_MARKETING_PACK_TYPES' instead of 'variant' singular, and the dashboard panel's own copy now says 'Posts all of this month's ... variants'. New test coverage in buffer-actions.test.ts: a 6-variant (3 facebook + 3 instagram) fixture asserting all 6 get queued in order with the correct (i/n) labels and exact per-call createBufferUpdate text, plus a partial-failure case asserting only the failed variant is labeled failed while its sibling variant for the same profile still reports scheduled. The pre-existing single-variant-per-type test needed no changes — the (i/n) suffix is only added when a profile has more than one matching variant, so its assertions (`result.scheduled` equals bare profile ids) still hold. Verified: npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.json (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npm test (2652 passed, up from 2650 — 2 new, 198 files unchanged) + a full clean rebuild (`rm -rf .next && npm run build`, clean, same 42-route ○/ƒ split) + npm run dev sanity check (/, /dashboard/leads, /docs/marketing-automation all 200; curled the rendered docs HTML and confirmed the new 'queues every matching' prose is present; dev server killed, local.db deleted afterward). NEXT_STEPS unchanged — all five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked; this is a sold-capability wiring-gap bug fix discovered by audit in an already-shipped scaffold, not a resolution of any gated item. Diff-gate anchor stays at dda421a (targeted spot-check, not a full tier 1-5 sweep).",
